1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:05,060
If your chest looks flat no matter how much you train, this video is for you.

2
00:00:05,360 --> 00:00:05,940
Here's the thing.

3
00:00:06,240 --> 00:00:09,750
Your chest isn't one big muscle you can just push harder.

4
00:00:10,050 --> 00:00:11,260
It has three parts.

5
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:14,810
The upper chest, which gives you that full, lifted look.

6
00:00:15,110 --> 00:00:18,010
The middle chest, which builds thickness and size.

7
00:00:18,310 --> 00:00:21,920
And the lower chest, which draws that sharp line at the bottom.

8
00:00:22,220 --> 00:00:25,240
Miss one of them, and your chest will never look complete.

9
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:27,090
So let's train all three.

10
00:00:27,390 --> 00:00:28,600
Let's start at the bottom.

11
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:29,780
The lower chest.

12
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:32,230
Almost nobody trains it on purpose.

13
00:00:32,530 --> 00:00:36,400
And without it, your chest just fades out with no clear edge.

14
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:39,130
The best exercise for it is dips.

15
00:00:39,430 --> 00:00:42,300
Find two parallel bars and grab them firmly.

16
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:44,730
Lean your upper body slightly forward.

17
00:00:45,030 --> 00:00:49,160
That small lean is what puts the work on your chest instead of your arms.

18
00:00:49,460 --> 00:00:52,080
Bend your elbows and lower yourself slowly.

19
00:00:52,380 --> 00:00:55,110
Stop when your shoulders reach the height of your elbows.

20
00:00:55,410 --> 00:00:56,700
Then push back up.

21
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,000
That's one rep.

22
00:00:58,300 --> 00:01:00,320
Do three sets of eight to twelve.

23
00:01:00,620 --> 00:01:04,120
If that feels easy, slow the reps down or add weight.

24
00:01:04,420 --> 00:01:05,330
No bars at home?

25
00:01:05,630 --> 00:01:06,990
Do incline push-ups.

26
00:01:07,290 --> 00:01:10,590
Put your hands on a chair or a bed, shoulder-width apart.

27
00:01:10,890 --> 00:01:15,250
Squeeze your core and your glutes so your body forms one straight line.

28
00:01:15,550 --> 00:01:17,840
Lower yourself over two to three seconds.

29
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:19,330
Then push back up.

30
00:01:19,630 --> 00:01:22,040
Three sets, as many reps as you can.

31
00:01:22,340 --> 00:01:23,980
Next, the middle chest.

32
00:01:24,280 --> 00:01:25,710
This is your foundation.

33
00:01:26,010 --> 00:01:28,710
And the king here is the dumbbell bench press.

34
00:01:29,010 --> 00:01:32,030
Lie down on a flat bench with a dumbbell in each hand.

35
00:01:32,330 --> 00:01:35,400
Keep your elbows at about forty-five degrees from your body.

36
00:01:35,700 --> 00:01:38,130
Too wide, and your shoulders take the stress.

37
00:01:38,430 --> 00:01:40,640
Too close, and your triceps do the work.

38
00:01:40,940 --> 00:01:45,330
Plant your feet, push your chest up, and press the weights over your chest.

39
00:01:45,630 --> 00:01:49,160
Then lower them slowly, until you feel a deep stretch.

40
00:01:49,460 --> 00:01:51,300
Three sets of eight to twelve.

41
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:53,500
At home, do deep push-ups.

42
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:57,350
Put your hands on two stacks of books, or on push-up handles.

43
00:01:57,650 --> 00:02:00,490
This lets your chest go lower than the floor would allow.

44
00:02:00,790 --> 00:02:02,680
More stretch means more growth.

45
00:02:02,980 --> 00:02:05,630
Go all the way down, then all the way up.

46
00:02:05,930 --> 00:02:07,760
Three sets, close to failure.

47
00:02:08,060 --> 00:02:10,780
And finally, the most important one for looks.

48
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:12,070
The upper chest.

49
00:02:12,370 --> 00:02:15,150
This is what makes your chest look full in a t-shirt.

50
00:02:15,450 --> 00:02:17,460
Use the incline dumbbell press.

51
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:19,910
Set the bench to about thirty degrees.

52
00:02:20,210 --> 00:02:22,310
Not higher, or your shoulders take over.

53
00:02:22,610 --> 00:02:24,580
Press up, then lower slowly.

54
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:28,210
If you feel the top of your chest burning, you're doing it right.

55
00:02:28,510 --> 00:02:30,350
Three sets of eight to twelve.

56
00:02:30,650 --> 00:02:31,340
No equipment?

57
00:02:31,640 --> 00:02:32,720
Decline push-ups.

58
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:35,620
Put your feet on a chair and your hands on the floor.

59
00:02:35,920 --> 00:02:39,140
Now your body angle shifts the work to your upper chest.

60
00:02:39,440 --> 00:02:41,240
Three sets, close to failure.

61
00:02:41,540 --> 00:02:44,700
Now, three mistakes that will kill your progress.

62
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:50,330
One. Bouncing the weight. Control every rep, especially on the way down.

63
00:02:50,630 --> 00:02:55,450
Two. Flaring your elbows. Keep them at forty-five degrees to protect your shoulders.

64
00:02:55,750 --> 00:03:01,590
Three. Doing the same reps forever. Every week, add one rep, or a little weight.

65
00:03:01,890 --> 00:03:02,610
Here's your plan.

66
00:03:02,910 --> 00:03:04,580
Train your chest twice a week.

67
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:06,690
Dips or incline push-ups.

68
00:03:06,990 --> 00:03:08,980
Dumbbell press or deep push-ups.

69
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:11,500
Incline press or decline push-ups.

70
00:03:11,800 --> 00:03:12,820
Three sets each.

71
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:15,260
But none of this works without one thing.

72
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:16,440
Consistency.

73
00:03:16,740 --> 00:03:17,990
Not one perfect week.

74
00:03:18,290 --> 00:03:19,650
Months of showing up.

75
00:03:19,950 --> 00:03:22,250
Do that, and your chest will grow.

76
00:03:22,550 --> 00:03:26,060
Subscribe to Linework Fit, and I'll see you in the next one.
